  "Question": "What is the value of the following expression? \\[\\dfrac{\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{7}{8}}{\\frac{4}{5}}\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1 \\)",
    "B": "\\( \\dfrac{25}{16} \\)",
    "C": "\\(2 \\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{43}{20} \\)",
    "E": "\\(\\dfrac{47}{16} \\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The long fraction bar divides the entire numerator by \\(4/5\\), so first add the fractions on top. Their denominators are equal:\n\\[\n\\frac38+\\frac78=\\frac{10}{8}=\\frac54.\n\\]\nDividing by the nonzero fraction \\(4/5\\) means multiplying by its reciprocal, \\(5/4\\). Thus\n\\[\n\\frac54\\div\\frac45\n=\\frac54\\times\\frac54\n=\\frac{25}{16}.\n\\]\nThe value is \\(\\frac{25}{16}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
